{
 "note": "R104 - in-payload references of team-art / kit members on NHL Legacy X360 (`.rx2`, `\\x89RW4xb2`) and PS3 (`.rpsgl`, `\\x89RW4ps3`)\n(review 2026-09-25 R97-R101, next task). Read-only. Sources: the loose `rendering/**` files of each Legacy tree (R103b showed nameplate /\nrink-logo loose files byte-identical to the unwrapped archive members; this probe re-checks that identity on a sample of EVERY family\nbefore relying on the loose copy) and `fe/ion/artassets/teamlogos/t{id}.big` (FE crest containers).\n\nParsed reference fields (RW4 container, big-endian; layout decoded on six members and then applied to every member, refusing on mismatch):\n  header      0x00 magic 8 | 0x20 u32 file_count | 0x30 u32 file_table_offset | file table = file_count x 24 B\n              {u32 offset | u32 0 | u32 size | u32 align | u32 type index | u32 type id}; type id 0x10031 / 0x10030 = raw raster payload\n              (offset relative to the header size), 0x20003 = raster descriptor, 0xEC0010 = name dictionary.\n  manifest    `00010004 | u32 n (4) | n x u32 offsets (relative to the manifest)`; sections found by their type word:\n              0x10005 types {u32 count | u32 12 | u32 0 | count x u32 type id}; 0x10006 external arenas {u32 count | u32 dict off |\n              u32 0 | count x u32 arena id | ...}; 0x10007 subreferences {u32 count | u32 dict off | u32 0 | u32 a | u32 b | u32 0};\n              0x10008 atoms {u32 count | ...}. Located by scanning 0x40..0x400 for the manifest word (one hit required).\n  names       0xEC0010: {u32 count | u32 w1 | count x {u32 string abs offset | u32 type id | u32 object index} | NUL strings}\n              (w1 = 0x1505 observed; verified per member: offsets inside the chunk, string order, object index -> a 0x20003 chunk).\nChecks per member: external arena ids (distribution across all members), subreference count, atom count; every dictionary name, its\ntokenised numbers vs the member's own id tuple from its path (self-name) - any name whose numbers name ANOTHER id is a cross-reference\ncandidate; SCOPED search over the non-payload bytes (header, manifest, descriptors, dictionary - raster payloads excluded, where a\n4-byte match is noise): (a) ASCII occurrences of other team-art stems (`texlib_`, `name_`, `sock_`, `logo_`, `centerlogo_`, `puck_`,\n`t<digits>.big`) outside the dictionary strings, (b) djb2 (EB path hash, R99) of every team-art member path of the tree, as a\nbig-endian u32 - hit count against a random expectation. A negative search result is a scoped negative, not proof of absence.\nFE crest `t{id}.big`: container magic, inner member names (BIG4 / EB listing), numbers inside the names vs the crest id.\nUsage: python r104_team_art_payload_references.py <out.json>\n",
